This repository contains all the versions of the Rubik's Cube Solve Tracking system.
It also contains the testing software for the system.

To run the system, download the most recent YOLO model weights by downloading the runs folder (the code automatically selects the most 
recent weights), and the cube_tracker_V63.py file. This is the most recent version of 
the tracking system.

Open the cube_tracker file in terminal. You may be required to install various libraries such as numpy, OpenCV, and ultralytics.
Once all are installed, the tracker can be run. Make sure that the installed libraries, YOLO weights, and cube_tracker file
are in the same folder and the terminal is running within that folder

To run the testing files, install both the cube_lab_new.py and the atp_runner_new.py files. Make sure they are in the same folder as
the other installed files. Run the files to test the various systems.
